  "scientific_scope_status": "For k positive formula-indexed rates lambda_i<=b, let q_i=1-lambda_i/b and acquire a certified q_star>=max q_i. Independent geometric extras P(G_i=m)=(1-q_i)q_i^m followed by H|G ~ Gamma(k+sum_i G_i, rate b) reproduce the full law of sum_i Exp(lambda_i). Geometric index skipping and thinning query rates only at candidates, with expected k q_star queries; an equivalent rational-envelope compound-Poisson route is provided. The source reports internal proof and separate internal reconstruction, not external correctness or a newly invented gamma-series identity.",
